{"posts":[{"id":27406,"name":"Satadru Bag","username":"deltasata","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/deltasata/{size}/3482_2.png","created_at":"2025-08-12T20:08:47.589Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...equest, which limits how many transients I can process daily. So I am looking for a more efficient way. Questions: Will the Prompt Products Database (PPDB) contain any images or small cutouts? If not, what about the small cutouts that would be sent in alert packets to brokers? Are these not stored in PP...","post_number":1,"topic_id":10800},{"id":23383,"name":"Roy Williams","username":"roy","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/roy/{size}/1254_2.png","created_at":"2024-08-15T08:45:56.209Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...m not clear what it is. I understand it will be implemented as a TAP service (is that right?). If so, when might there be a prototype? What is in the PPDB that is not in the collection of recent alerts? I think there is something about improved orbits for solar system bodies, is that right? Anything on...","post_number":1,"topic_id":8978},{"id":10583,"name":"Melissa Graham","username":"MelissaGraham","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/melissagraham/{size}/2549_2.png","created_at":"2019-08-02T16:01:17.835Z","like_count":3,"blurb":"...tudy’s findings, any decisions will be announced, e.g., in the solicitation for full proposals. Q7. How do users access the Prompt Products Database (PPDB) when they are working with alerts via a community broker? External entities (e.g., brokers) may interface with the PPDB via the Web API aspect of th...","post_number":1,"topic_id":3780},{"id":28217,"name":"Alec Koumjian","username":"alec_b612","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a698b9/{size}.png","created_at":"2025-10-27T15:58:08.501Z","like_count":3,"blurb":"Hello hard working Rubin data product teams, I am curious if there is a regularly updated timeline for the PPDB and Alert Stream? It is absolutely understood that timelines need to shift over time, but it would be good to be able to anticipate when data product...","post_number":1,"topic_id":11162},{"id":30592,"name":"Carrie Holt","username":"carrieholt","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/carrieholt/{size}/4213_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-01T18:49:22.765Z","like_count":1,"blurb":"...catalog in the data releases? If it is different, do you know when we will have an idea what that schema will be? I remember talk of it being in the PPDB, but it is not currently in the sdm-schema site: https://sdm-schemas.lsst.io/ppdb.html Thanks!","post_number":1,"topic_id":12222},{"id":10929,"name":"Andy Salnikov","username":"andy_slac","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/andy_slac/{size}/1726_2.png","created_at":"2019-11-20T18:09:34.403Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...e aware of this move but still want to (and have to) make this known to wider community. I’m planning to complete the long process of renaming of dax_ppdb package into dax_apdb today. Motivation for that move is described in https://jira.lsstcorp.org/browse/RFC-642 RFC-642 . All or most of the dependent...","post_number":1,"topic_id":3938},{"id":29028,"name":"Natasha Abrams","username":"nsabrams","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/838e76/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-02-06T19:02:10.329Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...fying questions about the prompt product database vs what’s in the alerts. Do all DIASources become alerts? If not, will all the DIASources be in the PPDB even if they’re not associated with an alert? For the DIAObjects in the table, are there more datapoints than what would have been included in the al...","post_number":1,"topic_id":11546},{"id":11263,"name":"Stephen Smartt","username":"ssmartt","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/c2a13f/{size}.png","created_at":"2020-02-18T22:28:38.634Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...available, 24hrs ? For how long will such forced photometry be run ? The whole survey ? Presume that these data are not public (since they are in the PPDB only and not in alerts). A strong science case for accessing forced photometry after detection of a transient is fast declining transients e.g. kilon...","post_number":1,"topic_id":4044},{"id":25680,"name":"Melissa Graham","username":"MelissaGraham","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/melissagraham/{size}/2549_2.png","created_at":"2025-05-27T00:33:06.410Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"...cenzo, thanks for this question. In the future, once Prompt Processing and Alert Production is running at full fidelty, the Prompt Products Database (PPDB; DiaSource, DiaObject, and associated tables for forced photometry and moving object) will be updated within 24 hours (i.e., new table rows become av...","post_number":2,"topic_id":10106},{"id":30880,"name":"Frossie Economou","username":"frossie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/frossie/{size}/9_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-27T19:27:54.051Z","like_count":10,"blurb":"...books in a way that you won’t lose your work if that happens. :new: New alert retrieval by ID service Services built on our prompt products database (PPDB) will be our next major release. In the meanwhile, we have a new service that, provided you know one of our Alert IDs (by subscribing to your favorit...","post_number":1,"topic_id":12345},{"id":30881,"name":"Melissa Graham","username":"MelissaGraham","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/melissagraham/{size}/2549_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-27T19:32:15.645Z","like_count":6,"blurb":"...S Data Access Center (Section 3.3 of https://rtn-011.lsst.io/ RTN-011 ). What other Rubin data is coming out this year? The Prompt Products Database (PPDB), promptly-processed images, and the “Full” DP2 release of raw, visit, and difference images are all expected by the end of 2026. The exact timeline...","post_number":1,"topic_id":12346},{"id":30763,"name":"Jake Kurlander","username":"Gerenjie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/gerenjie/{size}/4228_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-11T16:44:28.023Z","like_count":1,"blurb":"...d be using to check the most recent association for a diaSourceId? There should eventually be a solar system table in the prompt processing database (PPDB) which includes updates to the initial alert state, but it doesn’t exist yet.","post_number":14,"topic_id":12204},{"id":30608,"name":"Leanne Guy","username":"leanne","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/leanne/{size}/622_2.png","created_at":"2026-07-02T01:22:18.557Z","like_count":1,"blurb":"...dated information on the delivery schedule and contents of Data Preview 2, the phased release of prompt data products, and the initial version of the PPDB together with an update on data access services. DP2 schedule: DP2 will be delivered in two phases. Early DP2 (EDP2), will be released on 2026-07-27...","post_number":1,"topic_id":12224},{"id":30240,"name":"Igor Andreoni","username":"iandreoni","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/iandreoni/{size}/3124_2.png","created_at":"2026-06-02T21:37:06.833Z","like_count":3,"blurb":"...s to make Solar System processing pipeline outputs more accessible to the RSP user community as a stopgap measure until the Prompt Products Database (PPDB) is delivered. Rubin Solar System data products are small relative to the full astrophysical transient data volume, and bridging this gap would subst...","post_number":1,"topic_id":12064},{"id":29782,"name":"Melissa Graham","username":"MelissaGraham","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/melissagraham/{size}/2549_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-14T17:33:11.427Z","like_count":1,"blurb":"...a that will be part of DP2. AFAIK, a live version of the Promptly-processed visits metadata will only be available when the Prompt Products Database (PPDB) comes online later this year.","post_number":2,"topic_id":11868},{"id":29849,"name":"Еrіс Веⅼⅼⅿ","username":"ebellm","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/ebellm/{size}/771_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-22T16:12:11.191Z","like_count":2,"blurb":"Hi @jrob93 , DetectorVisitProcessingSummary is not populated at the moment, but it would only be available in the future in the PPDB (or a similar RSP-accessible database) rather than the alerts. It is a detector-level table.","post_number":2,"topic_id":11899},{"id":29789,"name":"Leanne Guy","username":"leanne","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/leanne/{size}/622_2.png","created_at":"2026-04-14T22:33:25.967Z","like_count":1,"blurb":"...tions timeline. DP2 is still on track for a July - September 2026 release. The delivery date for Prompt image and catalog products, and access to the PPDB has slipped slightly to between June and September 2026. An update is also provided on the start of the LSST.","post_number":1,"topic_id":11873},{"id":28801,"name":"Meg Schwamb","username":"mschwamb","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/mschwamb/{size}/3007_2.png","created_at":"2026-01-08T09:22:36.263Z","like_count":0,"blurb":"Thanks, Leanne. “Due to ongoing technical development, the PPDB is not expected to become publicly available before June 2026. Further details will be provided in future versions of this document.” Will February a...","post_number":2,"topic_id":11434},{"id":28640,"name":"Lynne Jones","username":"ljones","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/ljones/{size}/1804_2.png","created_at":"2025-12-08T01:03:44.023Z","like_count":2,"blurb":"...downloads of the exposure information from a user-specified range of nights, on some timeframe (currently not well defined, but might be sooner than PPDB). And we could just re-start the creation of the opsim-format databases like we did during SV. I haven’t heard any objections to creating the databas...","post_number":4,"topic_id":11342},{"id":28451,"name":"Melissa Graham","username":"MelissaGraham","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/community.lsst.org/melissagraham/{size}/2549_2.png","created_at":"2